Test basic functionality of the sync command

  $ kitchensync() { RUST_BACKTRACE=1 $TESTDIR/../target/debug/kitchensync $* ; }

  $ mkdir a
  $ cd a

  $ echo hello > hello
  $ echo world > world
  $ kitchensync update
  # updating
  A ./hello
  A ./world
  # update successful

Now sync to a new directory

  $ mkdir ../b
  $ cd ../b

  $ kitchensync sync ../a
  # syncing from ../a
  get "../a/.ksync" -> ".ksync.remote"
  A ./world
  A ./hello
  # sync successful

  $ cat hello
  cat: hello: No such file or directory
  [1]

Make a change in a and sync again

  $ cd ../a
  $ echo "hello world" > hello
  $ kitchensync update
  # updating
  # update successful

  $ cd ../b
  $ kitchensync sync ../a
  # syncing from ../a
  get "../a/.ksync" -> ".ksync.remote"
  # sync successful

  $ cat hello
  cat: hello: No such file or directory
  [1]

Test deleting files

  $ cd ../a
  $ rm world
  $ kitchensync update
  # updating
  D ./world
  # update successful

  $ cd ../b
  $ kitchensync sync ../a
  # syncing from ../a
  get "../a/.ksync" -> ".ksync.remote"
  # sync successful
